        "in224": "The original image is resized to 224 x 224 exactly as for the first pass; the window is cut from this image and resized to the network inputs. The second-pass map is pasted at the original resolution. The second pass therefore sees the lesion at the canonical scale but receives no pixel that the first pass did not receive.",
